{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Duplicate/RCA disposition before close.\n\nStep 0(a): tracker sweep for `dict(os.environ) pytest fixture secrets environment leak` found closed canonical `broadish-permanent-condor` for this same `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py::box` fixture leak and closed sibling `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran` for the broader class. Step 0(b): no report version in this duplicate; using created_at floor gives origin/main floor a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5, with no later changes to `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py`. Step 0(c): worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/credleak-fixtures` at e768151d680f7295bfd37424cec31946b88d0ab8 (= origin/main).\n\nProven root cause: this ticket is not a new live defect. It is a duplicate of already-landed `broadish-permanent-condor`: prior RCA showed pre-fix commit parent of 034e17209c had `box` returning a nested full `dict(os.environ)`, and pytest default-long fixture rendering could print a first-position synthetic ambient sentinel. Current origin/main has the established fix pattern at `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py:177-187`: a narrow mutable allowlist (`PATH`, `STATE_DIR`, `DEPLOY_REPO`, `COMPOSE_DIR`, `MIRROR_DIR`, `HEALTH_TIMEOUT`) rather than a full environment copy.\n\nProof/replication: `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin \"$PWD/.venv/bin/python\" -m pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py` was included in a focused run of all affected surfaces; result `72 passed, 1 skipped in 97.73s`. The original sentinel-rendering report no longer reproduces. Construct sweep: an AST scan of all `tests/**/*.py` found no `@pytest.fixture` returning `dict(os.environ)`, `os.environ.copy()`, or a nested alias to either. Remaining raw-env strings are security-test fixtures/strings or non-fixture subprocess-env work covered by `antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch` per the canonical RCA.\n\nDefect origin/Gerrit: canonical fix is Gerrit Change 1847, commit 034e17209c9b30dad3aa08971a10b71f39fd5547, reachable from origin/main with trailer `rebar-ticket: fc43-3c50-ec6c-4a3e`; prior ticket records LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and merged CI run 32101886011. Because this ticket is a duplicate rather than an independent defect fix, the durable origin is the `duplicates` edge to `broadish-permanent-condor`, not a new `caused_by` edge."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788231696575240615,"uuid":"aa4f5628-7637-4c15-b700-6aaad79d1b03"}